# Note: raising COALESCE_ROWS to 8 left the 7-period row check unable to tell a block's first
# and eighth tiles apart (all 64 blocks of 8 had a repeated scale). The sweep's '0/64 wrong'
# at factor 8 was therefore a slightly weaker check; the harness rows above use period 13.
